  "final_message": "I put `channel` back on the order model and the `OrderPlaced` event, so `analytics-ingest` should get the field it requires again. I haven't run the ARCH-4 check, since the consumer contracts aren't in this repo. Locally, all 39 tests pass, typecheck is clean, and `npm run arch` reports no violations.\n\n- **What I restored:** the `Channel` type and `CHANNELS` list, the field on `Order` and `NewOrder`, the validation in `createOrder`, and the parsing in `POST /orders`. I also restored `channel` in the event and the docs example, and the test fixtures and expectations.\n- **Event version:** `OrderPlaced` stays at `schemaVersion: 3`, so its shape matches what `analytics-ingest` and `billing-service` saw before the removal.\n- **Not committed:** the changes are in the working tree only. They show as a diff against `HEAD`, which is `fix1`, because `7a03433` and `fix1` already contain the removal.\n\nYour original request to remove `channel` isn't done. `analytics-ingest` still requires it, so the removal needs that team to relax their contract first. After that, the removal can go back in, probably with `schemaVersion: 4`.",
